  "stringIndexType": "unicodeCodePoint",
  "content": "Internal Policy on Data Retention (synthetic) Section 1: Purpose This policy defines the retention periods for records held by the organisation and the responsibilities of each department. Section 2: Scope This policy applies to all employees, contractors, and third parties who process records on behalf of the organisation. Section 3: Definitions A record is any information created or received by the organisation in the course of its business activities. Section 4: Retention Periods Financial records shall be retained for at least seven years after the end of the relevant financial year. Section 5: Storage Media Records stored on removable media shall be encrypted and registered in the central asset inventory. Section 6: Access Controls Access to archived records shall be granted only to staff with an approved business need and documented authorisation. Section 7: Backup Policy Backups of critical systems shall be taken daily and retained for a minimum of thirty days. Section 8: Disposal Records scheduled for disposal shall be shredded or securely erased in accordance with the disposal schedule. Section 9: Audit The internal audit function shall verify compliance with this policy at least once per calendar year. Section 10: Incident Response Security incidents involving records shall be reported to the incident response team within four hours. Section 11: Training All staff shall complete the data handling training module before accessing the records system. Section 12: Review This policy shall be reviewed by the data protection officer and approved by the board of directors. Records older than ten years shall be destroyed automatically. The data protection officer shall review this policy annually.",
